    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "The entropy change for a mixture of the gases in any proportions moving towards the equilibrium position is also positive",
    "reading_order" : 46,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000047",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "Neither the forward nor backward reaction can go to completion as the entropy change from the equilibrium mixture to either the reactants or products is negative",
    "reading_order" : 47,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000048",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "At equilibrium, the total entropy change is zero",
    "reading_order" : 48,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000049",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "Δ*S*<sub>*total*</sub> [forward reaction] = Δ*S*<sub>*total*</sub> [backward reaction]",
    "reading_order" : 49,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "paragraph",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000050",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "The relationship between the total entropy of the reaction and the equilibrium constant (*K*<sub>c</sub> or *K*<sub>p</sub>) is",
    "reading_order" : 50,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000051",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "Δ*S*<sub>*total*</sub> = *R *ln*K*",
    "reading_order" : 51,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "paragraph",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000052",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "**Using total entropy change to calculate an equilibrium constant**",
    "reading_order" : 52,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "paragraph",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000053",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "Rearranging the equation mentioned above we get:",
    "reading_order" : 53,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000054",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "ln*K* = $\\frac{\\DeltaS_{total}}{R}$",
    "reading_order" : 54,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "paragraph",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000055",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "Hence:",
    "reading_order" : 55,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000056",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "*K* = $e^{\\frac{\\DeltaS_{total}}{R}}$",
    "reading_order" : 56,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "paragraph",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000057",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "**Relationship between equilibrium constant and equilibrium position**",
    "reading_order" : 57,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "paragraph",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000058",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "There is no hard rule for the relationship between equilibrium constant and the position of equilibrium",
    "reading_order" : 58,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000059",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "As a general rule, we can say a very large value of *K* suggests the equilibrium position is pushed towards the products (right-hand side)",
    "reading_order" : 59,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000060",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "Similarly, a very small value of *K* suggests the equilibrium position is pushed towards the reactants (left-hand side)",
    "reading_order" : 60,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  } ],
